<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ukraine decries 'horrific' Russian attack shortly after US envoys leave</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f9d0172ca272bcf75555fa61aacc3f36ef8b1aa085b4f595f74664315e93dd8</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T12:19:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-ukraine-decries-horrific-russian-attack-shortly-after-us-envoys-leave" /><summary type="html">Ukraine criticised Russia on Tuesday for launching a major missile and drone attack that killed at least two people shortly after a weekend visit by US envoys to both countries' capitals, where they tried to restart stalled talks on ending the war.</summary></entry><entry><title>Who are the Hindu group cited in Eiffel Tower staff walk out?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f322df006fb4d5dd3d66267a3c941f61333b160262fef92e89ef090c6a641ed</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T12:17:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-who-are-the-hindu-group-cited-in-eiffel-tower-staff-walk-out" /><summary type="html">The Eiffel Tower reopened on Tuesday after staff walked out over the removal of women colleagues during a visit by a Hindu religious group. The Bochasanwasi Akshar Purushottam Swaminarayan Sanstha (BAPS) spiritual movement later apologised for "any pain or inconvenience caused" by the incident. France 24’s Delano D’Souza takes a closer look.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia pounds Kyiv, ending three-day halt for US talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:751460eb67e95f9885a9b4764931397c3f6459eec74f0660ca89e79d055db2f1</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T11:35:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-russia-pounds-kyiv-ending-three-day-halt-for-us-talks" /><summary type="html">Russian missiles and drones pounded Kyiv overnight, killing two people and sending smoke billowing above the Ukrainian capital, ending Moscow's temporary halt to strikes on the city.</summary></entry><entry><title>In Ukraine, teens try to heal from trauma of war at summer camp</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b922526df2c9af2ef85f0b093800eddb81e2ad4be55fd0fc1e937d6b1c18ab21</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T11:10:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260908-in-ukraine-teens-try-to-heal-from-trauma-of-war-at-summer-camp" /><summary type="html">The psychological impact on the Ukrainian population of nearly five years of full-scale Russian onslaught is hard to overstate. Children and teenagers are particularly at risk of trauma. With support from foreign philanthropists, one Ukrainian NGO is trying to help at least a few teenagers cope better, via summer camps that mix therapy and fun. Our correspondent Gulliver Cragg reports.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Paris looks to profit as Céline Dion fans flock to French capital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:87570e22f095fc20a1979e2baba733bcb0f6fa7f230b74894cf0c46e7f2afb5a</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T10:32:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-paris-looks-to-profit-as-c%C3%A9line-dion-fans-flock-to-french-capital" /><summary type="html">Céline Dion’s hotly anticipated return to the stage is scheduled for this Saturday in Paris - the first of more than 16 concerts in the French capital in September and October. The shows mark a major milestone for 58-year-old Dion after years away from touring due to the rare neurological disorder. A total of 500,000 spectators are expected in Paris - a huge windfall for the economy, especially for the hotel, restaurant, and transport industries.</summary></entry><entry><title>France, South Korea pledge 1 billion euros to support cinema amid AI threat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:875a876d8ee2024c039e39ba54615d711d6577039a1af22ee568b32417104f4a</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T10:28:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-france-south-korea-pledge-1-billion-euros-to-support-cinema-amid-ai-threat" /><summary type="html">Hollywood star George Clooney and executives from US studios such as Sony Pictures and Disney were among the 200 guests that gathered in the south of France for a summit on the future of cinema on Monday. As part of the initiative, co-hosts France and south Korea have pledged 1 billion euros to safeguard against threats to the industry, particularly from AI.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Pheromone maxxing': Men avoid showers before dates to boost attraction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1551506449a61cb8ea30b51beb56fc0ca5c6f044b010d02753688cd230c44966</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:59:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260908-pheromone-maxxing-men-avoid-showers-before-dates-to-boost-attraction" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Tuesday, September 8: Papers discuss UK sanctions on Israeli settlements in the West Bank. Also, could AI change what it means to be human? Finally, "pheromone maxxing" is in; showers are out.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal’s Gen Z protests one year on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:426420bbc516469c6bb3c2efbf640219f799d558ebdad3123e030bb711067600</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:52:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-nepal-s-gen-z-protests-one-year-on" /><summary type="html">September 8 marks a year since a Gen Z-led violent revolt against corruption in Nepal forced the then prime minister to resign. The protests were triggered when government tried to suspend many prominent social media platforms for failing to comply with new Nepalese A year on, and as the country still grapples with the devastation caused by deadly floods, Morgan Ayre looks back at how Nepal got to this point and the challenges that lie ahead.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Truly terrifying’: AfD election win sparks protests across Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3c968655c9ad95085229a7f582b523af5b553cdfea678148171ae450ec48b28</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:50:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-truly-terrifying-afd-election-win-sparks-protests-across-germany" /><summary type="html">The victory of the far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) in Sunday's state election in Saxony-Anhalt sparked protests across Germany on Monday, as demonstrators called for a united front against the hardline anti-immigrant party. Some protesters call for the party, some of whose members have praised the Nazis, to be banned, but others say AfD's success is a result of a failure of mainstream political parties.</summary></entry><entry><title>London pub celebrates Bayeux Tapestry loan with ‘Beer Tapestry’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1de17c13df0bcba81d2cc7f3fce6455dcaacc9ed430fa76c6f68be5c64127ed</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:42:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-london-pub-celebrates-bayeux-tapestry-loan-with-beer-tapestry" /><summary type="html">Britons will finally get the chance to view the Bayeux Tapestry on home soil this week, as the 11th century work goes on display at the British Museum. And the exhibition has inspired a copycat tapestry, available to view for thirsty visitors seeking refreshment at a pub across the street.</summary></entry><entry><title>UAE leader warned Netanyahu of Hamas attack days before October 7, says report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:221b6f5524c39e8b37929654ff2ebec69ab3c5eb96ace0011076041dacfe31b4</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:40:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-uae-leader-warned-netanyahu-of-hamas-attack-days-before-october-7-says-report" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu faced strong backlash from opposition leaders on Tuesday after a report published by Haaretz newspaper said UAE President Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan warned Netanyahu that Hamas was planning a major operation days before the attacks on October 7. The report alleges that Netanyahu failed to inform security chiefs.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>French legionnaire escapes Colombian captors, makes four-day trek to freedom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbc19ba3d51699edf1ba3c52c0ddc519208914106408a3dd4371f641a3206f17</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:34:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-french-legionnaire-escapes-colombian-captors-makes-four-day-trek-to-freedom" /><summary type="html">A Colombian soldier in the French Foreign Legion who was taken hostage by guerrillas in Colombia escaped his captors after a four-day trek on foot through rebel-held territory. Jose Olger Melo Charry was taken hostage on August 6 by a dissident faction of the now-defunct FARC guerrilla group while he was traveling on a highway in Colombia's southwest.</summary></entry><entry><title>What is Germany's political 'firewall' and can it keep out the AfD?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7699f31650a8ce33469362e93e7684ead081ddd01143aba1ffb0ff0705f9b27f</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:26:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-what-is-germany-s-political-firewall-and-can-it-keep-out-the-afd" /><summary type="html">Alternative for Germany, or AfD, has established itself as a significant political force in the 13 years since its founding, but it has never been part of any state or federal government. That’s a result of what is often called a “firewall” against cooperation with the anti-immigrant, far-right party. France 24's Philip Turle explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia pounds Kyiv after pause for visit of US envoys</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3b0dbe94576846b6f5dd6e11626ef8f0f4b50bc3ce95673bd48746d234b3c22</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:23:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-russia-pounds-kyiv-after-pause-for-visit-of-us-envoys" /><summary type="html">Russia pummelled Kyiv with drones and missiles early on Tuesday, resuming its air attacks after a brief halt for the visit of US peace negotiators, killing two people and triggering fires across the Ukrainian capital. France 24’s correspondent in Kyiv Emmanuelle Chaze has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump threatens ban on Bombardier as Canada's retaliatory tariffs kick in</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe19126dbe495ba46dae53228b0fcaf2c679eae53dcb4836459a2037277dd48c</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:16:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260908-trump-threatens-ban-on-bombardier-as-canada-s-retaliatory-tariffs-kick-in" /><summary type="html">Canada's retaliatory tariffs of up to 50 percent on approximately $19.8 billion worth of US goods came into effect this Tuesday, further escalating the trade war between the two neighbours. At the same time, US President Donald Trump is threatening to ban sales of all Bombardier aircraft in the US, in spite of the Canadian company's deep web of US suppliers. Also in this edition: Iran raises the price of gasoline and French startup Mistral AI is now valued at €21 billion.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Houthi attacks disrupt Saudi oil facilities and wound more than 70</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f989b4f7147d51fef29950675dbef532b6e73aef518bbd983402b2b529a0cb0</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:14:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-houthi-attacks-disrupt-saudi-oil-facilities-and-wound-more-than-70" /><summary type="html">Attacks on Saudi Arabia Tuesday claimed by Yemen's Houthis wounded more than 70 people and ignited fires at several oil facilities and utilities in the kingdom's southern region, authorities said, in a major escalation in the renewed conflict between an important US ally and the Iranian-backed rebels.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Thieves steal works of art worth 9 million euros from France's Renoir museum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f2d8dd9ec9ed075d4830f0335ddb8b0cedd0656b80575bf82588fc30b048d31</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T08:36:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-thieves-steal-works-of-art-worth-9-million-euros-from-france-s-renoir-museum" /><summary type="html">Two thieves on Tuesday broke into the Renoir Museum in the town of Cagnes-sur-Mer in southern France and stole "four works of art", dropping one as they fled, according to the local mayor. Officials estimated the value of the stolen works at 9 million euros.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French AI startup Mistral valued at over 21 billion euros after latest funding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3d45da1910daa0b2a6a6f3c80b1732e838b41989ef0015c3abb11b11a71576d</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T07:03:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-french-ai-startup-mistral-raises-3-billion-euros-after-latest-funding" /><summary type="html">French AI company Mistral announced Tuesday that it had raised three billion euros ($3.5 billion) in what it described as the largest-ever European tech fundraising, valuing the startup at over 21 billion euros. While still an upstart compared to the AI giants OpenAI or Anthropic, Mistral says it is carving a niche by offering models that companies can run themselves with their own data.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal rescuers race to free dozens trapped in hydropower tunnels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:55105275d06fa3e50236c39deb09f9bb0f864d629465299ace11ab0c502c7130</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:51:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260908-nepal-rescuers-race-to-free-dozens-trapped-in-hydropower-tunnels" /><summary type="html">Authorities in Nepal on Tuesday said that rescuers are focusing on three hydropower project tunnels where they believe dozens of workers could be trapped. The announcement came two weeks after ​a devastating ‌flood killed that hundreds and left thousands missing in the Himalayan country and in ⁠neighbouring China's Tibet region.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Rubio kicks off tour in Latin America as US vies for regional influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2aaf662c599c8591bc3923b6edc28497e3da6f488dc8a479334e13d6799831fd</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T05:59:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-rubio-begins-latin-america-tour-in-colombia-to-secure-us-influence" /><summary type="html">United States Secretary of State Marco Rubio on Tuesday arrived in Colombia following the recent election of hard-right lawyer and US ally President Abelardo de la Espriella, and a string of right-wing electoral victories across Latin America. Colombia is the first stop on a tour designed to bolster pro-US leaders and cement influence over the continent.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: At least two killed in Kyiv as Russia renews strikes after three-day pause</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4907adfe53bda0eec705172f9e74cebdb94381d6cf1ae541c71814cc652c52aa</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T05:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-live-russia-resumes-strikes-on-kyiv-after-three-day-halt--c216aa8a2eec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-live-russia-resumes-strikes-on-kyiv-after-three-day-halt" /></entry><entry><title>Before Champions League, Kylian Mbappé campaigns for Ballon d'Or</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2088f457cf3b2aedbda43bbec075da591a07c2f423677b25fc40e3fbd9b63a76</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T05:22:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260908-before-champions-league-kylian-mbapp%C3%A9-campaigns-for-ballon-d-or" /><summary type="html">As the Champions League resumes, Real Madrid are hosting Inter Milan. Speaking at a press conference, Kylian Mbappé believes he has every chance of winning the Ballon d’Or.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Canada's counter-tariffs take effect on several US goods as trade war reignites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f84b42118e78405aa1ebe02d7011e7d7932897d53bee69b2841f5a183b26e700</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T04:03:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-canada-s-counter-tariffs-take-effect-on-several-us-goods-as-trade-war-reignites" /><summary type="html">Canada's counter-tariffs on billions of dollars in US products took effect Tuesday, as a trade war between the two countries heated up. Ottawa's pushback comes weeks after US President Donald Trump imposed 50-percent tariffs on a similar value of Canadian products, over what Washington deemed as "discriminatory treatment" against US alcohol, automobile and dairy industries.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump threatens to ban Canadian Bombardier jets from US market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:465b4f79800cc7a446032ab290873fafe0db39ad6ea90c21a57913e4d9a41031</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T02:24:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-trump-ban-canadian-bombardier-jets-us-market--64decde9a947.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-trump-ban-canadian-bombardier-jets-us-market" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump threatened on Monday to block sales of Canadian planemaker Bombardier in the United States unless it builds aircraft in the country, escalating trade tensions on the eve of Canadian retaliatory tariffs. Trump accused Canada of “unjust and unfair” trade practices but did not explain how a ban would work.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
